-- title:
--   Plane curve local ring is a DVR when partial_Y P≠ 0
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $P \in k[X][Y]$ be a polynomial in two variables, viewed as a polynomial in $Y$ with coefficients in $k[X]$, and assume $P$ is monic in $Y$. Let $a, b \in k$, and let $\mathfrak{m}$ denote the ideal of the quotient ring $k[X][Y]/(P)$ generated by the residue classes of the two elements $C(X - C\,a)$ and $Y - C(C\,b)$, that is, of $X-a$ and $Y-b$; it is assumed that $\mathfrak{m}$ is a maximal ideal. Assume further that the derivative of $P$ with respect to $Y$ does not vanish at $(a,b)$, in the sense that evaluating $\mathrm{derivative}\,P$ first at $Y = b$ and then at $X = a$ gives a nonzero element of $k$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a proof that the localisation of $k[X][Y]/(P)$ at the prime $\mathfrak{m}$ is an integral domain, together with, for that domain structure, the statement that this localisation is a discrete valuation ring. The existential packaging is needed because the discrete valuation ring predicate presupposes the domain instance.
--
--   This is the Jacobian criterion for a plane affine curve at the point $(a,b)$: nonvanishing of $\partial P/\partial Y$ there forces the local ring of $k[X][Y]/(P)$ at the corresponding maximal ideal to be regular of dimension one, hence a discrete valuation ring. It is used in [`ModularCurve.CharPModel.place_eq_of_ord_pos_of_derivative_evalEval_ne_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.place_eq_of_ord_pos_of_derivative_evalEval_ne_zero) in the analysis of places of a plane model of a modular curve in positive characteristic.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_CharPModel_isDiscreteValuationRing_localizationAtPrime_of_derivative_evalEval_ne_zero.lean

